🐛 Bug
Corner case where torch.baddmm(c, a, b) doesn't match torch.bmm(a, b) + c: if the inner dimension of a and b is empty, the result is zeros_like(c) rather than  c.
Easy to work around, but gives subtly wrong results, so maybe worth fixing.
To Reproduce
a = torch.zeros((2, 1, 0))
b = torch.zeros((2, 0, 1))
c = torch.ones((2, 1, 1))
torch.bmm(a, b) + c     # <-- ones((2, 1, 1))  (OK)
torch.baddbmm(c, a, b)  # <-- zeros((2, 1, 1)) (WRONG)
Possible Fix
The bug seems to be in bmm_out_or_baddbmm_ from aten/src/ATen/native/LinearAlgebra.cpp:
  // handle pathological cases that blas may not like
  if (self_or_result.numel() == 0) {
    return self_or_result;
  } else if (contraction_size == 0) {
    return self_or_result.zero_();       // <-- BUG for baddbmm
  }
Replacing that line with this seems to fix it:
    if (is_bmm_out) {
      return self_or_result.zero_();
    } else {
      return self_or_result.mul_(beta);
    }
